@baseUrl = https://localhost:5443
@contentType = application/json

### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Register a new (Viewer-role) user
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "manager@example.com",
  "password": "StrongPass123!",
  "confirmPassword": "StrongPass123!"
}

### Log in as the seeded admin (see appsettings.Development.json)
# The refresh token comes back as an httpOnly cookie, not in the JSON body — your
# HTTP client needs to keep cookies between requests for /refresh below to work.
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "ChangeMe123!Strong"
}

### List products (any authenticated role)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products?page=1&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Create a product (Manager or Admin)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "name": "Steel Bracket",
  "sku": "SB-100",
  "category": "Hardware",
  "quantity": 250,
  "price": 3.49
}

### Refresh the access token (uses the cookie set by /login)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/refresh

### Log out (revokes the refresh token and clears the cookie)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/revoke
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
